From 97bde9d8662adc9bbb09fbf9d45789f8681ac6e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Fix 'No exec result': handle built-in tool execs, wire-name
 collisions, fuzzy tool-id resume, parallel-call drain

Root causes found from production traffic on 15.204.94.214:

1. Cursor's agent harness dispatched its built-in tools (task, shell,
   read_file, list_dir, ...) as exec variants absent from the trimmed MVP
   proto. The oneof decoded to nil and handleExec closed the exec stream
   with no result, so the model saw the opaque 'No exec result' failure,
   retried, and gave up (client symptom: Task tool 'No exec result',
   subagent no return, directory reads with zero output).

2. Client MCP tools whose names collide with the built-ins (Task, Bash,
   Glob, Grep, Read, Write, ...) could bind to the unusable built-in of
   the same name.

3. Agent CLIs rewrite tool_call ids (call-<uuid>-N_<original>), so live
   session resume always failed with 'unknown or expired tool_call_id'
   and every tool round-trip rebuilt the run, losing the prompt cache.

4. decodeMcpArguments re-parsed every string argument as JSON, turning
   'true' into a boolean and JSON file bodies into objects, which failed
   client tool schema validation.

5. Only the first client tool call in a read batch surfaced before the
   segment paused, splitting parallel tool calls across turns.

Fixes:
- handleExec now answers unknown (built-in) exec variants with a
  model-readable throw naming the callable MCP tools, and logs the
  unknown proto field numbers.
- MCP tools that collide with built-in names are advertised under an
  mcp_-prefixed wire name and mapped back to the client name on emit;
  a run-request system directive plus action-text constraint steer the
  model to the MCP toolset.
- SessionManager resolves client-rewritten/sanitized tool_call ids by
  containment and normalizes them before SubmitToolResults, so live
  resume works and the prompt cache is preserved.
- fromProtobufValue keeps string arguments verbatim.
- readLoop now uses a persistent reader goroutine and drains for 120ms
  after the first tool call so parallel calls share one segment.
- StartSession retries once on transient run-open 5xx from Cursor edge.

Co-authored-by: Apologetic2022 <Apologetic2022@users.noreply.github.com>
